- **HIGH** — [§6 Service Flow](/Users/jamesgiroux/Documents/dailyos-repo/.worktrees/codex/v1.4.5-w4-c-dos-474/.docs/plans/v1.4.5-workspace-memory/L0-packet-W4-C-DOS-474.md:226) / [§10 Tests](/Users/jamesgiroux/Documents/dailyos-repo/.worktrees/codex/v1.4.5-w4-c-dos-474/.docs/plans/v1.4.5-workspace-memory/L0-packet-W4-C-DOS-474.md:376): the plan only asserts `WorkspaceFileKind::McpPlacement`. Current entity-seeded ingestion writes `document_entity_links` with `LinkAttributionSource::EntityIntake`, despite an existing `McpPlacement` attribution. Action: require the placement path to carry `LinkAttributionSource::McpPlacement` and add a test proving the persisted link attribution is `mcp_placement`.

- **HIGH** — [§1 PR Coordination](/Users/jamesgiroux/Documents/dailyos-repo/.worktrees/codex/v1.4.5-w4-c-dos-474/.docs/plans/v1.4.5-workspace-memory/L0-packet-W4-C-DOS-474.md:28) / [§8 Write Set](/Users/jamesgiroux/Documents/dailyos-repo/.worktrees/codex/v1.4.5-w4-c-dos-474/.docs/plans/v1.4.5-workspace-memory/L0-packet-W4-C-DOS-474.md:335): PR #355 changes the MCP handler interface to use `McpHandlerContext` and adds CI forbidding direct DB opens in handlers. The packet says “coordinate” but does not make the implementation conditional on the new signature or CI gate. Action: require `tool_placement.rs` to implement the post-#355 `invoke(ctx, actor, params)` shape when present and route DB/service access through `McpHandlerContext`.

